  <name>CFSSL</name>
  <summary>Cloudflare's PKI/TLS toolkit</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      CFSSL is Cloudflare's PKI/TLS swiss army knife. It is both a command line tool
      and an HTTP API server for signing, verifying, and bundling TLS certificates.
    </p>
    <p>
      CFSSL consists of a set of packages useful for building custom TLS PKI tools
      and multiple command-line utilities:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>cfssl - The main command line utility for certificate operations</li>
      <li>multirootca - A certificate authority server supporting multiple signing keys</li>
      <li>mkbundle - Build certificate pool bundles</li>
      <li>cfssljson - Takes JSON output from cfssl and writes certificates to disk</li>
      <li>cfssl-bundle - Build certificate bundles</li>
      <li>cfssl-certinfo - Extract certificate information</li>
      <li>cfssl-newkey - Generate private keys and certificate requests</li>
      <li>cfssl-scan - Scan hosts for security issues</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Key Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sign, verify, and bundle TLS certificates</li>
      <li>Generate certificate signing requests and private keys</li>
      <li>Support for RSA and ECDSA keys</li>
      <li>Certificate bundling with validation</li>
      <li>OCSP signing and serving</li>
      <li>Multi-root certificate authority support</li>
      <li>RESTful API server for certificate operations</li>
      <li>Certificate information extraction</li>
      <li>Host security scanning</li>
    </ul>
    <p><em>Usage Instructions:</em></p>
    <p>
      To use cfssl commands easily from your terminal, add the flatpak exports directory to your PATH:
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/share/flatpak/exports/bin:$PATH"' &gt;&gt; ~/.bashrc</code><br/>
      <code>source ~/.bashrc</code>
    </p>
    <p>Then access commands directly:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>com.cloudflare.cfssl version</code> - Main cfssl command</li>
      <li><code>flatpak run --command=cfssljson com.cloudflare.cfssl --help</code> - JSON processor</li>
      <li><code>flatpak run --command=cfssl-certinfo com.cloudflare.cfssl --help</code> - Certificate info</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All 8 binaries (cfssl, cfssljson, mkbundle, multirootca, cfssl-bundle, cfssl-certinfo, 
      cfssl-newkey, cfssl-scan) are available using <code>flatpak run --command=&lt;name&gt; com.cloudflare.cfssl</code>.
    </p>
  </description>
